      "writtenOn": "2024-12-26T18:26:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t have to calculate power for each channel separately if we intend just to return the combined power for all channels. This is because energy and power calculation is sample-based and does not depend on the values of previous samples (see the implementation here: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:system/media/audio_utils/include/audio_utils/power.h;l\u003d45;drc\u003d6386d8fa0d25d78b9239baa221f64cca84e8f36c). In other words, it\u0027s a linear operation. Thus, running `audio_utils_compute_power_mono` over an interleaved stereo input will produce the same result as running for each channel and then summing the result.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 409,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 419,
        "endChar": 88
      },
      "revId": "1f394269b5ceb88ca6538066f07b4957195092c7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a90f0727_72e8c181",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/vts/VtsHalDynamicsProcessingTest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 419,
      "author": {
        "id": 3538319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-27T12:26:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, then is it a good idea to change the function name audio_utils_compute_power_mono() to audio_utils_compute_power() and do the same for energy function?",
      "parentUuid": "68c6c56b_8ccebfff",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 409,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 419,
        "endChar": 88
      },
      "revId": "1f394269b5ceb88ca6538066f07b4957195092c7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3d44c004_510c00ad",
        "filename": "audio/aidl/vts/VtsHalDynamicsProcessingTest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 419,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-27T18:27:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There exist `audio_utils_accumulate_energy` which calculates energy per channel: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:system/media/audio_utils/include/audio_utils/power.h;l\u003d84;drc\u003d6386d8fa0d25d78b9239baa221f64cca84e8f36c. There is no similar `audio_utils_compute_power` for the moment, but if it were added I would expect it to be similar in action to `audio_utils_accumulate_energy`.\n\nAlso, technically `audio_utils_compute_power_mono` does calculate power for a single channel. It\u0027s just our understanding that due to how multichannel audio is represented and how energy calculation is defined, it is also possible to use it for non-mono layouts.",
      "parentUuid": "a90f0727_72e8c181",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 409,
        "startChar": 0,
